WEBVTT

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.860
Senpai...

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.580
Uh...

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.360
It's just...

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.800
You're still recovering, right?

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.860
I guess I couldn't ask you to...

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.640
Sparring?

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.120
If it's just a bit, I should be fine.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.370
Senpai...

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.000
Thank goodness.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:26.710
This should be a good chance.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.210
I can go all out,

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.380
right?

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.420
Itagaki-kun...

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.880
Hey, hey!

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.170
This is the Japanese Champion you're talking to!

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.400
That's not something a pre-debut rookie should be asking for!

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.760
Aoki-san!

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.570
It's fine.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:43.480
Let's fight seriously!

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:46.500
Thank you.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.490
All right,

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.710
I'll be your second.

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:54.490
Thanks.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.550
Ippo, you had better not lose.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:58.120
Okay.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:02.120
All right, start!

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:04.120
<i>He's cautious...</i>

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.120
<i>and very fast.</i>

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.500
<i>I don't really feel any pressure.</i>

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.840
<i>But still, he's the Japanese Champ.</i>

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.340
<i>Will my speed be effective on him?</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.680
Don't let him close in,

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:17.590
keep him at a distance with combos!

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:22.240
He's even faster than he was when he sparred against me!

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.270
Hell, he doesn't even need advice.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.140
<i>That stupid look on his face pisses me off.</i>

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:28.120
Don't let him touch you!

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.730
Put your kouhai in his place!

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:33.830
<i>I was going to get him when he drew his arm back,</i>

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:35.260
<i>but his backstep is too fast!</i>

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:35.950
<i>Yes!</i>

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.390
<i>He can't keep up with my speed!</i>

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.640
<i>Stay sharp and fast!</i>

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.990
<i>And make sure you stay out of reach when you're drawing your fist back!</i>

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.340
<i>His left is sharp!</i>

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.920
<i>If I throw too wide a punch, I bet I'd get nailed with a counter.</i>

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.420
<i>His boxing is elegant.</i>

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.920
<i>It's a lot like Miyata-kun's.</i>

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:55.800
<i>Below!?</i>

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:58.650
<i>The arm I blocked with is stinging!</i>

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.300
<i>If I had taken that, I would've been finished!</i>

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.600
Don't relax now!

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.030
The whole point of that was to get you to put your guard up!

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:05.790
<i>Oh, crap!</i>

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.730
<i>I stopped moving!</i>

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:12.820
<i>I can survive this!</i>

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:13.650
<i>I can see his punches...</i>

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:14.900
<i>I can dodge them!</i>

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:15.560
Stop!

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.400
You're going the wrong way!

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.370
<i>Why am I against the ropes?</i>

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:21.660
<i>Did he lure me here!?</i>

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.790
<i>What's up with this pressure!?</i>

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:27.330
<i>It's totally different from a minute ago!</i>

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:38.870
Man,

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:40.450
you really let him have it.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:41.620
Oh, no!

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:44.390
He was just so fast that I figured I had to get him before he got me.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:47.390
<i>All right, how do you like that, Takamura!?</i>

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.990
<i>I-Is that the attitude you should have as a second!?</i>

00:02:58.890 --> 00:02:59.690
Not yet...

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.560
The ten count...

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:02.700
isn't done yet.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:04.650
Itagaki-kun...

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:06.200
If you won't...

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.250
then I will.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.070
Huh?

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.720
Finally conscious?

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.060
Only going down four times in three rounds is pretty impressive.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.680
F-Four times?

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.900
<i>That's the Japanese Champ for you...</i>

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:27.260
<i>he's on a different level.</i>

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.220
Where'd senpai go?

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.670
He went back to the beach.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:33.030
Oh, I see...

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.940
I wanted to thank him for the help.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.070
You're a boxer-type, right?

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.150
Imitating a fighter like Ippo won't...

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.320
I'm not trying to imitate him.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.790
I'm trying to learn how to overcome him.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.820
Overcome?

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:46.630
Who?

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.940
It's me-dani!

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:51.470
Oh, it's Neko-chan.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:52.750
What's in the bags?

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.490
Makunouchi and the others are going back tonight-dani,

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:58.540
so I thought we could set off some fireworks tonight at the beach-daniyo.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.790
Fireworks?

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.260
Sounds good, doesn't it, Takamura-san?

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:04.440
Does...

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.490
Does it have to be at night?

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:08.910
It'd be kind of hard to see otherwise-daniyo.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:09.870
What's wrong?

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.570
It comes out...

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.690
on the beach.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:16.610
A super-dangerous poltergeist!

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.480
It tries to drag people into the ocean!

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.150
I've got proof!

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:20.900
Look here!

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:23.320
You can see where it grabbed me!

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:28.580
F-Fits like a glove-dani!

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:31.790
I was barely able to make it out of there!

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:35.020
You guys don't know what that kind of terror is like!

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:37.520
So there's something he's actually afraid of?

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.920
It'll be fine-daniyo.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.840
I'm sure they won't come out tonight-daniyo.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:41.760
No!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.000
I ain't going!

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:48.050
Takamura-san, the sun's setting!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.470
Let's go set off the fireworks!

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.000
Takamura-san!

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:53.480
Hang on a sec!

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:57.230
I've got a big one going!

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.920
Now that I think about it,

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.020
I made it out of the sea in one piece.

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:04.540
I guess I don't have anything to fear from ghosts after all.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.240
Yeah! {jama: added}

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:15.650
<i>Phew...</i>

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:19.050
<i>Even for me, this is one masterpiece of a turd.</i>

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:23.580
There's a hair-like thing sticking out of my crap.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:24.260
What is it?

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:31.680
What the hell is this thing!?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:33.570
Did this come out of my body!?

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:34.270
How!?

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:35.780
Why!?

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:37.560
Is this part of the curse!?

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.200
Am I cursed!?

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:46.970
It's pretty.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:48.320
Yes.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.040
How is it?

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:50.830
Pretty relaxing, right?

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:51.610
Right!

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:52.780
Thank you very much!

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:56.540
All right, we're setting this one off-daniyo!

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.180
B-Be careful not to get burned!

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:14.060
I-I'll be careful.

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:17.740
I guess nothing happened between them after all.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:20.640
Even though they spent the night together...

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:21.450
Hey!

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.300
You started already?

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.070
Let us join in!

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.290
You guys are late!

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.280
Where's Takamura-dani?

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.050
I guess he didn't want to come.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.110
He said something about being cursed.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:36.210
Oh, he's not coming?

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:38.910
Well, no reason we can't have a great time...

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.290
without him!

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:43.460
Yeah, no sense in worrying about someone who decided not to come.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.920
Let's get it started-daniyo!

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:46.800
Yeah! {jama: added}

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:51.130
There's something about the beach that makes me feel carefree.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:52.050
Hell, no!

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.260
It's because you-know-who isn't here.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:55.720
No need to worry about any trouble this time.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.370
Imagine if Takamura-san was here...

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:58.270
You got that right!

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.320
<i>Aoki and Kimura...</i>

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:05.480
<i>they get the death sentence.</i>

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:10.510
<i>Ippo and Itagaki don't seem to miss me either...</i>

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:11.280
<i>they're accomplices.</i>

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:13.780
<i>Enjoy yourselves while you can.</i>

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.040
<i>I'll drop you from heaven straight to hell!</i>

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:23.950
<i>What?</i>

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.510
<i>They're duds!?</i>

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:26.800
<i>I'm really unlucky lately!</i>

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.370
Takamura-san!

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:35.870
You came after all!

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:37.990
Crap, he might've heard us.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.600
Gotta smooth this over.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.300
So you did want to join in-dani!

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.270
No need to be so awkward-dani!

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:45.770
D-Don't put it that way!

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.160
Bad idea!

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:51.270
See, now he's sulking.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.860
Do something, Ippo!

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.820
B-But he's probably mad!

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:57.050
It's fine.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.040
I'll just go back.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.650
If I stick around, it'll just be trouble, right?

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:04.330
I bet I'm just a pain!

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.890
He did hear us.

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:07.990
Now what? If we don't deal with this now...

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:09.340
Please don't go back!

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:11.840
Come shoot the fireworks with us!

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:13.340
I'm leaving!

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:15.860
Please don't say that!

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.560
Itagaki-kun, back me up!

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:21.300
If you're not here, it won't feel right!

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.060
We'd be lonely without you, Takamura-san!

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:25.260
Quit trying to butter me up!

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:28.150
You were all enjoying yourselves earlier!

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.320
You're right, it was fun.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:33.430
But something was missing...

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:36.360
Our feelings weren't united,

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:40.370
because our leader wasn't here to guide us.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:41.760
That's right!

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:43.750
We can't really start until our leader is here!

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:44.370
Boss!

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.370
Captain!

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.290
Trying to build me up after all this...

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:07.510
Dammit...

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:24.750
I guess you do need me after all!

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:28.910
Hang on a second!

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:30.060
Leave that for later!

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.120
There's an order to setting off fireworks.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.990
Ippo, get those ready!

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:34.460
Right!

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:36.160
Man, you guys are so helpless!

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:37.990
And that's why you need me!

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:39.230
You need me!

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.990
Now he's ordering us around.

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:43.260
Just let him.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:45.600
That was amazing, Itagaki-kun.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.350
You managed to cheer up Takamura-san.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.930
Well, I've always had a way with words.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:52.870
With girls too?

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:55.740
Could you give me some pointers on how to talk to them?

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:59.150
Senpai, you've already got a wonderful girlfriend!

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:00.520
You can't say that after what you two did last n—

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:03.490
You're too loud, and we didn't do anything!

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:06.720
Hey!

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.620
We're setting off the big ones!

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:09.500
Okay! {jama: added}

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:21.270
They're going off without a hitch-dani.

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:23.510
It reminds me of you all-daniyo.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:27.110
Fireworks in the night sky...

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:28.650
Boxers in the ring...

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:33.520
In the world of professional sports, boxers have the shortest careers-dani.

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:39.090
They pour all their youth into it and bloom briefly, but brilliantly.

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:43.040
The fact that it burns out so quickly is part of why it's so beautiful-daniyo.

00:10:44.550 --> 00:10:49.040
Hopefully, you all will burn brightly and brilliantly for as long as possible-dani.

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:51.160
Nekota-san...

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:54.560
Don't compare us to a bunch of cheap fireworks.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:56.550
We're the stars that are above them!

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:59.340
And we're gonna keep shining!

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:01.950
I'm that big one!

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:05.540
I'll become the world champion so you can always look up at me!

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:06.620
Stars, huh?

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:08.190
Pretty poetic there, Leader.

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:11.310
Then we're those stars over there!

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:12.270
Right!

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:15.580
Our goal is the Japanese Title!

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:17.030
<i>A goal, huh?</i>

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:18.570
<i>Then my goal is...</i>

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:21.610
<i>to get a firm grip on the baton I received from Date-san.</i>

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:25.070
<i>And to one day fight Miyata-kun.</i>

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:31.700
The spirit of the Kamogawa Crew is burning bright-dani!

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:33.880
That's the spirit everybody-daniyo!

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:38.370
All of you, become brilliant shining stars-daniy-

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:41.420
Nekota-san!

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:48.470
Duck!

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:48.470
Kumi-san!

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:49.390
Everybody run away!

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:50.850
Why are we under attack!?

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:51.740
Look out, Tomiko!

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:53.770
Masaru!

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:54.330
Aoki!

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:55.250
You did this, didn't you, Takamura-san!?

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.160
I don't know what you're talking about!

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:07.830
Geez, it's so hot.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.600
There's no way I can train when it's this hot.

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:14.330
The coach is still out of town and the guys from the training camp haven't come back either.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:18.230
This is god's way of telling us to take a nap.

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:19.460
Ain't that right, Ippo?

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:24.550
Did you say something, Aoki-san?

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:26.590
Working hard as ever, aren't you?

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:29.050
What are you lying around for, Aoki!?

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:30.720
C-Coach!

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:33.000
We got a request for a spar with you.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.170
Are you up for it?

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:35.760
A spar?

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:38.100
They asked us to help them out.

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.570
They should be here any time now.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:41.280
It's fine with me,

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.230
I'm warmed up already.

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:47.360
He's a rookie who hasn't debuted yet, but he's got quite a reputation.

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:48.280
Right.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:51.870
Sorry we're late.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:53.580
Our friends from the Otowa Gym have arrived.

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:56.480
Thanks for helping us out today, Kamogawa-san.

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:58.100
We appreciate it.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.960
<i>So he's my sparring partner.</i>

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:04.470
<i>He seems like he would be pretty strong.</i>

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:12.980
Um... Hello...

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:15.850
I'm Imai Kyosuke!

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.280
Thank you very much for helping me out today!

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.070
I-Imai-kun, is it?

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.480
It's nice to meet you.

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:28.030
This is spectacular!

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:30.320
I idolize you, Makunouchi-san!

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:33.440
Being able to trade blows with my idol is an honor!

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:36.330
And more than anything, I want to test my strength!

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:39.830
I intend to make the most of today and go all out!

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:43.050
<i>Where did I hear that recently?</i>

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:46.130
Listen, you... quit grinning like a goofball.

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:49.380
He's a newbie and he wants to spar with the champion?

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:51.710
I can't think of it as anything other than underestimating you.

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:54.020
I said he was an up and comer. {Solo-  A what?  Line is missing something}

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:58.980
His record as an amateur was 35 matches, 35 wins, 33 RSC's.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:58.980
Note: RSC = Referee Stopped Contest, the amateur equivalent of a TKO.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:02.260
He was the national inter-high champion two years in a row.

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:04.750
If he debuted as an 8-rounder, he would still do well.

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:06.980
That's even better than Itagaki.

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:08.780
Be sure not to underestimate him.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:10.180
Right!

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:12.590
Sorry for the wait.

00:14:12.590 --> 00:14:14.120
We're ready to go.

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:17.040
Then let's get started.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:21.420
<i>From his build, I'd say he's a fighter-type.</i>

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:23.420
<i>For now,</i>

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:25.740
<i>I'll see what he can do.</i>

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:34.390
<i>He's fast!</i>

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:36.680
<i>What a quick step-in!</i>

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.140
<i>And his punches are heavy!</i>

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.640
<i>I'll go to the side.</i>

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:42.360
<i>He managed to catch me!</i>

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:44.610
What're you doing, Ippo!?

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:47.940
<i>A fighter who chases you down if you try to get away...</i>

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:49.860
<i>I have to push him back with punches!</i>

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:56.740
All right!

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:57.920
Nice body blow!

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:59.620
He's buckling over!

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:05.580
He fought back!?

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:08.340
He said that he looked up to him, and it's true that they're very similar.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.560
It's not mere imitation either.

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:12.370
He's making full use of that style!

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:13.970
He's strong.

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:16.120
<i>That was...</i>

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:17.860
<i>If I hadn't been wearing headgear...</i>

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.010
<i>He's incredible...</i>

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:21.980
<i>I can't believe he hasn't even debuted yet!</i>

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:28.480
Third round's over!

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:29.490
That's enough!

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.600
Thank you so much.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:36.010
I learned a lot.

00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:40.690
<i>It was just sparring,</i>

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:42.500
<i>but I actually tried to beat him.</i>

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:44.500
<i>I got drawn in by his intensity.</i>

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:48.500
<i>He's already got the attitude of a professional.</i>

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:53.100
<i>If he got some more experience and showed up as a challenger...</i>

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:54.510
What's up!

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:56.530
We're all wrapped up!

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:57.990
We're back!

00:15:57.990 --> 00:15:59.770
Huh, you were sparring?

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:00.770
Yeah,

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.890
and Ippo got his ass kicked by a rookie.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:04.650
Senpai got his ass kicked?

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:06.770
That's impossible!

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:09.780
Kyosuke!

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:11.780
Manabu?

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:13.710
What? They know each other?

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:14.780
Seems that way.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:17.530
You joined the Kamogawa Gym?

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:28.040
I see you're the same as you were in high school.

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:31.910
It's fine if you haven't made it past that.

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:34.550
I'm going after my goal as a pro,

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:37.940
and I'll be taking the shortest route possible...

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:40.430
to Makunouchi-san's title.

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:42.930
You'll never make it that far.

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:46.100
You won't make it to senpai.

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:47.440
Because this time...

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:49.940
I'm going to stop you!

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:55.470
H-Hey, Kyosuke!

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:57.730
T-Thanks for today!

00:16:57.730 --> 00:16:58.450
Kyosuke!

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:03.700
Why couldn't I say anything back!?

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:07.710
<i>Itagaki-kun...</i>

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:14.720
I first fought against him at a national tournament.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:17.920
The second I saw him, I knew...

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:20.110
he had to be strong.

00:17:20.110 --> 00:17:20.780
Well,

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:24.230
he does seem more like a martial artist than an athlete.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:25.930
You get scared?

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:26.750
No.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:28.180
I was excited.

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:30.230
Because if I had won, I'd be number one.

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:32.190
But...

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:39.350
When I woke up, I was laid out on the ground.

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:41.100
It was a total loss.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:43.160
During high school...

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:45.780
we fought three times, and I was KO'd every time.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:46.940
But this time...

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:48.080
Ippo.

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:50.290
What do you think?

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:52.280
What do you mean?

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:54.150
You sparred with both of them, right?

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:56.370
Who do you think is stronger?

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:59.340
Um... Well...

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:02.260
I... Um... That's....

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:04.210
I know already.

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:07.700
I don't stand a chance against him right now.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:09.270
That's why... {jama: added}

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:13.060
I chose the Kamogawa Gym because it has the reputation of being tough.

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:15.780
Well, this worthless guy...

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:19.280
managed to keep winning and became champion against all odds!

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:23.620
Imai's gonna be a seed in the Rookie King Tournament next year, right?

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.520
That'll be your chance for revenge!

00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:27.290
Right!

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:29.530
I'll win the Rookie King Tournament!

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.050
I found it.

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:35.550
This is it.

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.920
The Rookie King Tournament... How nostalgic.

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:41.930
<i>Itagaki-kun and Imai-kun...</i>

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:45.040
<i>If you just look at boxing fundamentals, Itagaki-kun should have the advantage.</i>

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:48.260
<i>He's faster and has better instincts than Imai-kun,</i>

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:50.570
<i>but, he's still missing something...</i>

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:00.860
<i>It's happening!</i>

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.280
<i>It's finally happening!</i>

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:07.080
<i>Takamura-san's world title match!</i>

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:12.330
Congratulations, Takamura-san!

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:13.680
There you are.

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:15.150
I ran all the way here!

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:18.500
We thought it was delayed, but Takamura-san has his title shot back!

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:20.020
After all this time...

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:21.750
Huh?

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:23.090
You don't seem very excited.

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:26.100
You don't think it's weird?

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:29.550
Well, I was surprised it was so sudden...

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:31.130
It was sudden all right...

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:34.110
The gym just got a call from the champion's manager.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:39.190
They said they could set up a title match in December.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:40.210
December!?

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:41.320
Great! {jama: added}

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:43.490
So he might be the champion before the year is ov-

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:44.740
Before!?

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:48.450
B-But Takamura-san has a match in October!

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:50.390
He won't have any time to get ready!

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:51.570
They did it on purpose.

00:19:51.570 --> 00:19:53.850
They made the offer knowing that...

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:57.380
he's gonna have two matches in two months and will have to stay a Jr. Middleweight the whole time.

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:00.810
They're taking how rough Takamura-san's weight management is into consideration...

00:20:00.810 --> 00:20:02.630
Pretty sneaky of them.

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:05.130
Maybe we should pass this up and then wait until he's in his best condition.

00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:06.390
Ippo...

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:10.140
I'm ready to go right now.

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:12.210
Takamura-san...

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:15.770
He knows what he's doing.

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:17.770
The WBC...

00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:21.000
World Jr. Middleweight Champion...

00:20:21.810 --> 00:20:24.280
Bryan Hawk.

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:25.940
Takamura-san...
